cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these replication materials, please cite the paper."
title: >-
  Replication materials — The Information Costs of Climate Misinformation:
  Evidence from Global Financial Data
abstract: >-
  Replication code and derived data for a study of whether daily variation in
  the distributional character of climate misinformation moves firm-level
  information costs. Misinformation is measured as the KL divergence of the
  day's misinformation-score distribution from a stable background
  distribution, built from a five-model LLM ensemble over ~265,000 classified
  climate posts, and merged onto a 19.2 million row global firm-day panel.
authors:
